<title>SWITZERLAND: Roche H1 net profit rises 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Roche H1 net profit rises 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     2,428	     vs 2,213</p>
<p> Group operating profit     2,057	     vs 1,953</p>
<p> Group gross profit	   6,272	     vs 5,390</p>
<p> Non-operating income	 926		 vs 786</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the Swiss pharmaceuticals group is Roche Holding AG. On average analysts had forecast a six-month net profit of 2.45 billion Swiss francs, an increase of 10.9 percent. Forecasts ranged from 2.05 billion to 2.75 billion.  </p>
<p>Operating profit as percent</p>
<p> of sales, in percent	 22		  vs 25</p>
<p>Net profit as percent of  sales, in percent	    26		  vs 28</p>
<p> Research, development	1,416	     vs 1,128</p>
<p>R&amp;D as percent of sales,</p>
<p> in percent		     15		  vs 15</p>
<p> Sales (announced July 15)  9,302	     vs 7,769</p>
<p> Cost of sales		  3,031	     vs 2,379</p>
<p> Operating costs		4,215	     vs 3,437</p>
<p> Taxes			    527		 vs 502</p>
<p> Minorities		     28		  vs 24</p>
<p>Balance sheet June 30 vs December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Total assets		   45,025	    vs 37,776</p>
<p> Shareholders equity	  22,675	    vs 20,780</p>
<p> Current liabilities	  5,697	     vs 5,434</p>
<p>Long-term debt, non-current</p>
<p> liabilities		    15,678	    vs 12,241</p>
<p>-- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
